GITLO LICENSE (freeware) - English translation

Copyright © 2026 Imam MAASSOU. All rights reserved.

Gitlo is **proprietary software distributed free of charge** (freeware). This license grants you the right to use it;
it does not transfer ownership of it to you. By installing or using Gitlo, you agree to these terms.

## 1. What you may do

- Install and use Gitlo **free of charge**, on as many devices as you like.
- Use it for **personal or professional** purposes, including at work and on commercial projects.
- Share the **unmodified official installers**, free of charge, stating where they come from
  ([gitloapp.github.io](https://gitloapp.github.io/) or the [GitHub releases](https://github.com/IMAMx39/gitlo-releases/releases)).

## 2. What you may not do

- Sell, rent or charge for Gitlo, or include it in a paid offering.
- Modify, decompile or disassemble Gitlo, or attempt to obtain its source code, except to the extent that applicable
  law expressly permits it.
- Remove or alter copyright notices.
- Use the Gitlo name or logo for another product, or suggest an endorsement by the author.

## 3. Third-party components

Gitlo includes open source components (Flutter and Dart packages), each under its own license: MIT, BSD or Apache 2.0.
Their authors and license texts are listed [further down this page](https://gitloapp.github.io/en/license/#third-party). Those components are governed by their
own licenses, not by this one.

## 4. Your data

Gitlo runs on your machine and works on your repositories with the `git` installed on your system. It only contacts an
online service in these cases:

- checking for updates, with GitHub (can be turned off in Settings › Updates);
- the hosting services (GitHub, GitLab, Gitea…) and the AI provider you choose to connect;
- author avatars, fetched from the hosting service (can be turned off).

Your access tokens stay in your system keychain. The author does not collect any usage data.

## 5. No warranty

Gitlo is provided **"as is"**, without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular
purpose or freedom from errors. Gitlo runs real git commands on your repositories: keep backups and push your work
regularly.

## 6. Limitation of liability

To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, the author shall not be liable for any damage, direct or indirect,
arising from the use of or inability to use Gitlo, including loss of data or code.

## 7. Changes to this license

The author may change this license for future versions of Gitlo. A version already released remains governed by the
license it was released with.

## 8. Termination

If you do not comply with these terms, your right to use Gitlo ends automatically. You must then stop using it and
delete your copies.

## Contact

For questions about this license, or for a use it does not allow, open an
[issue on GitHub](https://github.com/IMAMx39/gitlo-releases/issues).

*This is a translation. The French version is the reference text.*
